<svg class="science-svg ifu-svg" viewBox="0 0 520 400" role="img" aria-labelledby="ifu-title ifu-desc">
  <title id="ifu-title">From an instrumental velocity gradient to a dynamical mass</title>
  <desc id="ifu-desc">
    Two synthetic steps. Slice bias: a compact source seen through the IFU image slicer; light falling off-centre within each slice shifts that slice's spectrum, so an apparent velocity gradient appears although no gas motion is put in. Dynamical mass: a rotation velocity and radius give the total mass inside that radius; because the mass scales with velocity squared, an instrumental gradient left in the data inflates it.
  </desc>
